// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ending E3 "Kerrid, last off the wall" (C, 2 min). GOODBYE: KERRID. act3_ending.md §2
// E3; ADR 0020 (e); ADR 0022 (g). He has been coming apart since H09, slowly, from the rope-burns on his hands outward
// (released THEN, like everyone: rule 7); his motes RISE throughout (glimmer_lift; no held light in the last farewell).
// He looks over the rail at the sea once, the way a captain checks a stair, and REPORTS: "Stair's clear." (a report,
// not a release). Then, to Rhen, a small thing. Dry and plain, gallows humour, no speech. He fixes Rhen's collar the way
// he grabbed it at Corrow. His own rising light throws HIS SHADOW across the deck onto Rhen's feet: for a moment the
// shadow is clearer than the man. The camera stays at Rhen's height; framed with Rhen only (rule 8). T-08 (optional
// insert): if ch19_learned_the_hitch, Kerrid sees the hitch on Rhen's wrist line before he goes; no line.
// `goodbye_kerrid`: a solo low string with a gamelan pulse, the walking rhythm slowing to a stop.
title: ending_kerrid
location: ch18/kite
---
@letterbox on
@camera E07
@music goodbye_kerrid fade=2.0
@vfx glimmer_lift at=kerrid_hands count=20 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@mark kerrid kite_rail walk
@anim kerrid look_at sea
@wait 4.0
Kerrid [neutral]: Stair's clear. #line:ending_kerrid_001 #tn:"The Corrow stair-watch's all-clear: a captain's report, not a farewell."
@wait 3.0
<<if $ch19_learned_the_hitch>>
    @camera E08
    @anim kerrid look_at rhen_hitch
    @wait 3.0
<<endif>>
@camera E07
@anim kerrid fix_collar rhen
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [soft_smile]: Stand up straight. Your father slouched. #line:ending_kerrid_002
@wait 3.0
@vfx glimmer_lift at=kerrid count=60 motion=spiral_up rate=slow
@anim kerrid shadow_on rhen
@wait 8.0
@letterbox off
===
